{
  "requirement": "The view of {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes` MUST use\nthe current workspace source at book-render time and explicitly identify its\ncontents as current workspace source notes.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. The notes view must use the current workspace source at book-render time. It must also explicitly identify its contents as current workspace source notes.\n\nThe test `src/execution_coverage/notes.rs#mod[tests]/fn[each_render_reads_current_notes_and_keeps_recorded_reviews_without_writing]` covers both.\n\n- **Current source at render time:** The test renders once with \"Original platform explanation.\" in `code.rs`. It then rewrites `code.rs` with \"Updated platform\" and renders again. The second render must contain \"Updated platform explanation.\". The part of the content before \"Review:\" must not contain \"Original platform explanation.\". A cached or stale implementation would fail both assertions. The `render` helper calls `pages` directly with the real path, so it exercises the actual view generation.\n- **Explicit identification:** The test asserts the content contains \"Current workspace source notes\". `pages` emits this string in a header that says \"**Current workspace source notes**, read at book-render time\". The assertion checks the label, and the label is in the generated page.\n\nThe sibling obligations (`render_only` and the reviews behavior) are not part of this subject. The test also checks that the saved review file is unchanged and that no `target` directory is created. That is extra and harmless.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "34cd489e9583ec89defb29da4f6e03551162cf88ab1742ab0c0582e7c24b9ca8",
